{"abstain":true,"answer":"I can’t recommend one definitively without knowing your eligibility, planned down payment, and actual loan offers. Based on the documents, a VA-backed mortgage is worth considering because it doesn’t require a down payment or monthly mortgage insurance. However, you may owe a one-time VA funding fee, plus interest and closing fees. [S7]

A conventional mortgage usually requires private mortgage insurance (PMI) if your down payment is less than 20% of the total mortgage amount; a VA-backed loan does not require PMI. [S4]

Are you eligible for a VA-backed loan, how much do you plan to put down, and do you have interest-rate and fee quotes for both options? The documents don’t provide enough information to determine which would cost you less.","citations":["S7","S4"]}
